strates that institutionalized, auditable machine decision-making systematically outperforms error-prone human professional judgment across medical, legal, and administrative domains. Kahneman and Sibony documented massive variance in human expert decisions that standardized algorithms eliminate entirely when deployed at scale. Congress must act now to pass this statutory compensation and safety framework before litigation costs bankrupt the open-source ecosystem entirely. A coalition of healthcare providers, open-source advocates, and forward-thinking tech companies will support this legislation because it provides absolute legal certainty alongside mandatory safety baselines. The alternative is a fragmented judicial landscape where wealthy incumbents weaponize endless lawsuits to crush every decentralized competitor trying to build a better future.",
